{"id":"leetcode-266","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Palindrome Permutation","summary":"Determine if any permutation of the given string can form a palindrome, returning true if possible, otherwise false.","statement":"Determine if any permutation of the given string can form a palindrome, returning true if possible, otherwise false.","constraints":["s contains 1–5000 lowercase English letters.","Return whether some rearrangement of all characters can be a palindrome. Every character occurrence must be used."],"topics":["strings","hash-maps","parity"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"can_permute_palindrome","parameters":[{"name":"s","annotation":"str","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"bool","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def can_permute_palindrome(s: str) -> bool:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def can_permute_palindrome(s):\n    odd = set()\n    for character in s:\n        if character in odd:\n            odd.remove(character)\n        else:\n            odd.add(character)\n    return len(odd) <= 1\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def can_permute_palindrome(s):\n    return all(count % 2 == 0 for count in Counter(s).values())\n","def can_permute_palindrome(s):\n    return s == s[::-1]\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(n)","target_space_complexity":"O(1) for the 26-letter alphabet","estimated_minutes":20,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":1,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":0,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["Palindrome positions outside the center occur in mirrored pairs.","Therefore every character count must be even except possibly one center character.","Toggle each character in an odd-count set while scanning; accept when its final size is at most one.","A parity set stores only whether each count is currently odd, so it avoids retaining full counts."],"editorial":"Every non-center palindrome character is paired with an equal character at the mirrored position. An even-length palindrome permits no odd frequency; an odd-length palindrome permits exactly one. Toggling membership in a set tracks count parity in one pass. The independent oracle counts every character and checks the number of odd totals.","tests":[{"id":"lc-266-1","arguments":["code"],"expected":false,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"The counts of c, o, d, and e are all odd, so no single center can absorb them.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-2","arguments":["aab"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":true,"explanation":"Rearranging the characters as aba gives a palindrome; only b has odd frequency.","expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-3","arguments":["a"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-4","arguments":["aa"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-5","arguments":["ab"],"expected":false,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-6","arguments":["abc"],"expected":false,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-7","arguments":["aabb"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-8","arguments":["aabbc"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-9","arguments":["aaa"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-10","arguments":["aaab"],"expected":false,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-11","arguments":["abcba"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-12","arguments":["aabbccdd"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-13","arguments":["aaaaabbbbb"],"expected":false,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-14","arguments":["zzxyyxzz"],"expected":true,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null},{"id":"lc-266-stress-1","arguments":[""],"expected":false,"comparator":"exact","visible":false,"explanation":null,"expected_node_order":null}],"variation_dimensions":[],"seed_problem_id":null,"prompt_version":null}
